  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.8: \"Could not ask\" is no longer reported to the product as \"no licence\" — a new LicenseResult.Unavailable carries the transient case (User Panel not running, channel silent, client-side rate limit) separately from a platform denial, so a product can stop gating features forever and stop prompting to buy a licence the user already owns. The cached verdict now has its own per-product store keyed by ProductKey: offline works without an active lease and survives a restart, which previously it did not for free products. The on-disk cache record is merged rather than replaced by whichever writer touched it last — lease renewal no longer erases ProductKey and the offline expiry, which used to break offline degradation from the very first renewal. A cached status is raised only on proof, never by default. The panel's answer budget is now derived from the channel timeout (IpcProtocol.HandlerBudgetMs) instead of being an independent number, so the panel cannot think for longer than the product is willing to wait. Half-connectivity (captive portal) is read as absence of network rather than as a server denial.\nv2.1.7: Offline grace now lasts the full period the server signed (cacheValidUntil, 7 days) instead of being cut to 24 hours by the live-path replay window; a failed signature or integrity check no longer deletes the cached licence, so a single transient failure can no longer destroy the only offline artefact. Adds a second trusted central-key thumbprint, so replacing the signing key no longer requires every user to reinstall. Reports the plugin version to the platform on license validation (diagnostics only, no version gating).",
